{
  "results": [
    {
      "n": "G1",
      "evidence": "All five screenshots show the 3D scene rendered properly in Chrome without blank screens or visual errors.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "G2",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 2–5 confirm orbiting and zooming work; in the code, OrbitControls sets maxPolarAngle = Math.PI * 0.465 (keeping the camera above the tablecloth) and maxDistance = 15.5 (inside the 34x34 tablecloth).",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "G3",
      "evidence": "Once the one-time procedural canvas textures finish at startup, the runtime scene has modest vertex counts, instanced sugar meshes, two shadow maps (2048 and 1024), and lightweight Bloom + Bokeh passes, easily sustaining 30+ fps on a standard laptop.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "1",
      "evidence": "All screenshots display a bottom UI bar containing text ('Drag to orbit · Scroll to zoom') and two interactive buttons ('Macro DoF: ON' and 'Hero Angle').",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "2",
      "evidence": "The animate() function only updates OrbitControls, optional camera reset lerping, and BokehPass focus distance; there is no environmental motion in the scene.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "3",
      "evidence": "Screenshot 1 shows a close-up view from slightly above with the French toast stack centered on the dark plate, matching the framing and angle of the reference photo.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "4",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1–3 show three thick slices of French toast stacked and rotationally offset from one another, matching the reference photo.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "5",
      "evidence": "Banana slices are placed between the toast layers and around the stack on the plate in Screenshot 1, though several heavily intersect the toast geometry.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "6",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1 and 4 show blueberries clustered on top of the stack as well as scattered around the base on the plate.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "7",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1 and 5 show the stack resting on a dark round plate set upon a grey-brown cloth surface, though a black void is visible behind the cloth's edge at the top of Screenshot 1.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "8",
      "evidence": "White specks representing powdered sugar are scattered across the dark plate and lightly on top of the toast and berries in Screenshots 1 and 4.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "9",
      "evidence": "In Screenshots 1–4, the toast slices have uniform, repetitive vertical ridges all around their sides like giant fluted cookies or crackers rather than bread slices with rounded crust and soft cut edges.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "10",
      "evidence": "In Screenshots 1 and 4, the banana slices are round discs displaying a faint seeded pattern in the center.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "11",
      "evidence": "In Screenshots 1–4, the blueberries are round, vary slightly in size, and clearly show the indented star-shaped calyx crown.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "12",
      "evidence": "In Screenshots 1–3 and 5, some sugar specks hover in mid-air to the upper right of the top toast slice (`sugarInstanced` places specks in a radius up to 1.65 at y=2.66..2.78 regardless of toast bounds), and banana slices severely clip inside the toast rather than resting cleanly on surfaces.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "13",
      "evidence": "In Screenshots 1, 2, 3, and 5, the tablecloth plane ends visibly in the background, exposing a stark horizontal edge and empty black background above it.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "14",
      "evidence": "In the code (`keyLight.position.set(-5.2, 8.4, 5.4)`), the main window light comes from the front-left (+z) rather than behind-left, and in Screenshot 1 the syrup drips look dark brown with minimal warm highlights.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "15",
      "evidence": "Despite `BokehPass` being enabled (`maxblur: 0.0065`, `aperture: 0.00145`), Screenshot 1 shows the back rim of the plate and the tablecloth edge remain nearly sharp rather than softly blurred like the reference photo.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "16",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1–5 show soft contact shadows grounding the berries, banana slices, toast layers, and plate.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "17",
      "evidence": "At the very top of Screenshot 1, the area beyond the tablecloth is a solid, dark near-black void (`0x161412`) with no detail.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "18",
      "evidence": "In Screenshots 1 and 3, the syrup rivulets on the toast crust and puddles on the plate look like dark, semi-opaque brown plastic/chocolate rather than bright, translucent amber with crisp specular highlights.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "19",
      "evidence": "In Screenshots 1–4, the toast faces are smooth, uniform pale yellow-orange plastic-looking surfaces with regular striped brown edges, lacking uneven caramelised browning or porous bread crumb.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "20",
      "evidence": "In Screenshots 1–4, the blueberries have high-contrast blotchy light-blue and dark-blue patches with glossy plastic highlights rather than a subtle, dusty matte bloom.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "21",
      "evidence": "In Screenshots 1 and 4, the banana slices look flat, matte, and opaque, with dark grey shading artifacts from transmissive syrup meshes overlapping them rather than moist, slightly translucent fruit flesh.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "22",
      "evidence": "In Screenshots 1–5, the plate has a dark satin sheen, though it exhibits a strange bright circular ring artifact on its floor, and the tablecloth looks like a blurry grey-beige noise plane rather than distinct woven fabric.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "23",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1 and 5 show the plate and table surface are level without any unintended tilt.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "24",
      "evidence": "Inspection of `addCrustSyrupRivulets` and `animate()` shows the syrup meshes are completely static geometry with no dripping or running animation.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "25",
      "evidence": "Neither the screenshots nor the HTML source contain any steam or warm haze particle system or animation.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "26",
      "evidence": "There is no continuous environmental motion implemented in `animate()` at all.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "27",
      "evidence": "In Screenshot 4, all five blueberries on top share the exact same blotchy UV texture pattern, making adjacent berries look like obvious copies despite slight rotation differences.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "28",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1, 2, 3, and 4 show severe clipping everywhere: banana slices on top and between layers sink half-way into the toast meshes, and front banana slices clip right into the bottom toast slice and plate.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "29",
      "evidence": "In Screenshots 1–5, the sugar on the plate looks like coarse, uniform white polka dots/pellets rather than fine, soft powdered sugar.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "30",
      "evidence": "Screenshot 1 looks unmistakably like stylized/plastic 3D CGI with cracker-like fluted toast, coarse white dots, severe geometry clipping, and an on-screen UI bar, not passable for the reference photo.",
      "pass": false
    }
  ]
}
